# Backend Conventions

## Imports

- Logging: `from loguru import logger` — NEVER structlog
- Heavy AI/DB libs (`ultralytics`, `insightface`, `supervision`, `anthropic`, `qdrant_client`): lazy import inside methods
- Use `from __future__ import annotations` in every file

## Async patterns

- All DB operations use `AsyncSessionLocal` from `sentinel.db.base`
- CPU-bound work (YOLO, InsightFace) runs in `ThreadPoolExecutor` via `loop.run_in_executor`
- Event publishing: `await bus.publish(SentinelEvent(...))`
- Never block the event loop with synchronous I/O

## Type annotations

- All public methods must have return type annotations
- Use `AsyncSession` for DB session parameters
- Use `TYPE_CHECKING` guard for imports only needed by type checkers

## Error handling

- Camera readers: infinite loop with exponential backoff, never raise
- Pipeline processors: catch per-frame, log error, continue
- DB Writer: catch per-event, log error, never crash

## Config

- ALL settings via `sentinel.core.config.get_settings()` — never hardcode
- Device detection is automatic — don't assume mps/cuda
